## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

**10 tests audited · 1 Critical (systemic) · 0 High · 1 Medium · 0 Low**

This is a textbook **coverage-touching** test suite. Every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called (hence 95% coverage), but almost nothing is actually verified. Bugs in `UpdatePrice`, `ApplyBulkDiscount`, `ImportFromCsv`, `RemoveProduct`, `Search`, and `GetProductCount` would all slip through to production undetected.

---

### 🔴 Critical: Systematic Coverage-Touching (7 of 10 tests)

Every test follows the same pattern: call the method, skip verifying the outcome. The three tests that *do* assert only check `IsNotNull` — the weakest possible assertion.

| Test (line) | What it calls | What it asserts | What it should assert |
|---|---|---|---|
| `AddProduct_Works` (17) | `AddProduct` | **Nothing** | Product is retrievable afterward |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` (32) | `UpdatePrice` | **Nothing** | Price actually changed to 14.99 |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` (39) | `RemoveProduct` | **Nothing** | Product is no longer retrievable |
| `GetProductCount_Works` (63) | `GetProductCount` | **Nothing** | Count equals expected value |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (68) | `ApplyBulkDiscount` | **Nothing** | Each price reduced by 10% |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` (84) | `ImportFromCsv` | **Nothing** | Parsed product exists with correct fields |
| `GetProduct_Works` (24) | `GetProduct` | `IsNotNull` only | SKU, Name, and Price match input |
| `SearchProducts_Works` (46) | `Search` | `IsNotNull` only | Results contain "Widget", count is 1 |
| `GetAllProducts_Works` (55) | `GetAll` | `IsNotNull` only | List contains the added product |
| `ExportToCsv_Works` (77) | `ExportToCsv` | `IsNotNull` only | CSV string equals `"SKU-001,Widget,9.99"` |

#### Concrete fixes (before → after)

**`AddProduct_Works`** (line 17):
```csharp
// BEFORE
_catalog.AddProduct(product);

// AFTER
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(retrieved);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved.Price);
```

**`UpdatePrice_Works`** (line 32):
```csharp
// BEFORE
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);

// AFTER
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(updated);
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated.Price);
```

**`RemoveProduct_Works`** (line 39):
